### END Python.gitignore
### This repository
# repomix_output.md is a whole-repo dump used to hand the project to a model;
# infinite-mac is a large checkout mobile_api_check.mjs reads and is expected
# to sit here or beside the repo; sources/ was the old scratch directory the
# harnesses used before the archives moved into res/.
repomix_output.md
infinite-mac
sources

# reference/ is not published, and none of it is in git.
#
# It holds everything this project reads but does not own: Cythera itself and
# everything shipped with it, Apple's Inside Macintosh volumes, the game's own
# manual and hintbook, third-party applications, scraped fan sites and wikis,
# and text lifted out of the binary. This repository is public and served over
# GitHub Pages, so the whole directory stays on disk and out of git. Supply
# your own copy of the game and put it in reference/.
#
# Two things that used to live there are now at the top level precisely so they
# CAN be tracked: deprecated/ (retired work of ours) and delvmod/ (a submodule,
# so only a pointer is stored).
#
# It also stops a repeat of the 643 MB CD image that got committed here in
# August 2026 and made every push fail.
reference/

# tools/coldmap.py writes its output into the working directory, and all of it
# is derived from Cythera's own code -- a 7.2 MB disassembly listing, a function
# index, a call graph. The game is not ours to publish (see reference/ above),
# and the whole lot regenerates in about a second, so none of it is committed.
dis/
seg/
functions.txt
functions.json
classes.txt
xref_traps.txt
callgraph.txt
jumptable.txt
SUMMARY.txt

# Screen recordings of the real game (reference material for the port work).
# They are game footage and hundreds of megabytes; they stay on disk, out of git.
*.mov
*.mp4
*.m4v
*.webm

# The site's handoff is a working file for the local machine, not part of
# the published tree.
/NEXT-SESSION.md
